  "note": "Member in BRONZE, earnMultiplier 1. Order O-11001: line 1 is category PRODUCE amount 2000 and matches the 3x promotion, so it contributes 2000 x 3 = 6000; line 2 is category OTHER amount 1000 and matches nothing, so it contributes 1000 x 1 = 1000; the sum is 7000; 7000 / 100 = 70 points, so expectedPoints 70 and expectedLedgerDelta +70. The earn snapshots currencyUnit 100, line 1 multiplier 3 and line 2 multiplier 1. The rules are then changed to currencyUnit 50 and a 5x produce promotion. Return R-11001 returns 1000 of line 1 and all 1000 of line 2. From the stored snapshot the order's new worth is (2000 - 1000) x 3 + (1000 - 1000) x 1 = 3000 + 0 = 3000; 3000 / 100 = 30 points; the clawback is 70 - 30 = 40, so expectedPoints 40 and expectedLedgerDelta -40. Using the changed rules instead would recompute the new worth as (1000 x 5) / 50 = 100, which is why the snapshot is the only input a return may read.",
